{
  "dom_id": "step-q72713",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{2{cos}^{4}⁡x+2{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor $2{cos}^{2}⁡x$ from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{cos}^{4}⁡x+2{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)-1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)-1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡x-({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={cot}^{2}⁡x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{cos}^{4}⁡x+2{cos}^{2}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x-1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}={cot}^{2}⁡x-1\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
